if our cyberpunk lore series has got you  impatiently awaiting the arrival of  cyberpunk 2077 then you  are not alone to help you pass the time  we've compiled a list of great  cyberpunky books  movies and games for you to tuck into  you'll probably have guessed this one  would make the list but i highly  recommend checking out cyberpunk 2020  the dystopian tabletop game that forms  the basis for cyberpunk 2077.  originally written by mike pondsmith in  1988 the tabletop rpg covers an  alternative timeline of world events  occurring between 2013 and 2045.  as to the nature of those world events  well check out our extensive lore videos  but the game consists of 10 key roles to  choose from in character creation  difficulty values to contest with net  running and combat centered around  lethality there's no better place to  start than the game's fourth edition  cyberpunk red if you're a tabletop fan  waiting for 2077 to come out  ponsmith told dicebreaker that  bladerunner and walter john williams  double hardwired were inspirations for  cyberpunk though a number of people  assumed that william gibson's  neuromancer also helped spawn the  popular rpg  pondsmith didn't actually read  neuromancer until sometime later but  that doesn't mean  you shouldn't check it out neuromancer  burning chrome and mona lisa overdrive  are known together as the spawn trilogy  gibson's novels were published around  the mid-80s and look at a fictional  future where the world is ruled by  corporations  the novel also explores the unintended  consequences of rampant technology  including mind machine links the  evolution of ai and a global information  space  that gibson called cyberspace the term  had been used once before but not  in reference to a digital space gibson's  works are considered to be seminal  entries in the cyberpunk genre  that is alongside philip k dick's 1968  novel do androids dream of electric  sheep  which served as the narrative basis for  both blade runner films and is  responsible in large part for kicking  off the new wave science fiction  movement  and subsequently the cyberpunk sub-genre  his 1977 sci-fi novel a scanner darkly  was also  set in a dystopian future california and  was the basis for richard linklater's  2006 film of the same name starring  keanu reeves  two hemispheres of my brain are  competing  yes so there's another 2077 connection  for you there  if you're just not a book person no  worries there's plenty of cyberpunky  goodness to be found in more visual  mediums  look it goes without saying that you  should definitely watch the phenomenal  blade runner movies  but if you haven't already you should  also check out mad max fury road  apart from being in my opinion and  almost perfectly crafted film  it effectively captures the cyberpunk  subgenre staple of as bruce sterling  writes in the preface to gibson's book  burning chrome  a combination of low life and high tech  where technological advancements are  starkly contrasted against radical  social unrest  the locations and vibe of the original  mad max movies also serve as a great  primer for cyberpunk 2077's  badlands outside of night city and the  nomad path that kicks off there  fury road is also worth your time  because charlie's theron is super cool  almost everyone is aussie and a dude  plays a flame-throwing guitar on the  front of a speeding amp riddled truck  good movie as for what else you can  watch on the big screen check out ghost  in the shell  no not that ghost in the shell there we  go based on the manga of the same name  this 1995 anime cyberpunk film follows  cyborg public security agent  motoko kusanagi on her mission to hunt  down a hacker called the puppet master  in 2029 the narrative touches on themes  of philosophy  human identity and the implications of  technological advancements in really  fascinating ways  it's well worth a watch if you haven't  seen it or if you only caught the scarjo  one  but hey maybe your ideal prep before  playing cyberpunk 2077  is just to play other great cyberpunk  video games in which case your first  stop should be blooper teams observer  the critically acclaimed psychological  horror game follows detective daniel  lazarsky portrayed by none other than  rutger hauer well i'm not a vegetable  yet  lazarsky can hack other people's minds  in order to interrogate them and utilize  augmented vision to scan electronic  devices and biological evidence  the game is set in 2084 in krakow after  a devastating digital plague  gamespot reviewer david rayfield praised  the game's superbly detailed  environments  evocative sound design and the cyberpunk  story which he called one of the most  intriguing to be found in the genre in  years  when it comes to other tech heavy gaming  franchises there's probably one that  comes to mind first  deus ex deus ex first entry was  developed by ion storm in 2000.  the series continued over the 2000s with  invisible war  human revolution the fall and mankind  divided the games take place within a  future earth which is devolved into a  dystopian cyberpunk society  yeah another one multiple organizations  vie for control while the world is at  war with a nanovirus called the grey  death  in the middle of it all is our  protagonist nano augmented newbie agent  jc denton aside from its cyberpunk  narrative themes the gameplay is  designed to be flexible  across multiple gameplay styles it  incorporates styles across the action  role-playing  stealth and first-person shooter genres  much like cyberpunk 2077 there's an  emphasis on player choice  npc relationships and player agency  granted through the game's rpg elements  if turn-based rpgs are your thing it's  worth checking out the dense and  intriguing  shadow run series based on the tabletop  game of the same name  the game takes place in a cyberpunk  fantasy world in 2054 and you play as a  shadow runner much like cyberpunk's  shadowrunners are mercs for hire  surviving on skill and instinct and must  navigate a world  ruled by mega corporations shadowrun  gained traction from its pen and paper  roots by blending the vastly popular rpg  with the most popular sci-fi media other  honorable mentions in the video game  realm  include watch dogs if what you're really  after is that hacking fix  flying wild hog cyberpunk fps hard reset  for shooter fans  and cyberpunk narrative adventure the  red strings club which should state  those who like to talk the talk  in a deep neon cyberpunk world with  plenty going on beneath the surface  let me know down in that comment box  what your favorite cyberpunk  books movies and games are and between  this and our cyberpunk lore series we'll  have you all ready to go for 2077 by the  time it releases  we'll see you again soon
 

